<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Etiuda</displayName>
  <description>Team folder, team lead's key, version checks, Etiuda Studio's AI service, and the accounts on a managed computer</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_Etiuda">Etiuda</string>
      <string id="EtiudaCat">Etiuda</string>
      <string id="TeamFolder">Set the team folder</string>
      <string id="TeamFolder_Explain">This policy setting specifies the folder from which Etiuda reads the team file on this computer.

If you enable this policy setting, enter a full path, such as D:\Team\share or \\server\team. Etiuda reads the team file from this folder. A value that is not a full path is ignored, and Etiuda keeps the folder it already uses.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the folder is chosen on the desk when it joins the team.

If both this setting and "Set the team lead's key" are configured and either value is not valid, Etiuda uses neither.</string>
      <string id="LeadKey">Set the team lead's key</string>
      <string id="LeadKey_Explain">This policy setting specifies the public key of the team lead whose team file Etiuda trusts on this computer.

If you enable this policy setting, enter the lead's public key as 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters, as it appears in the team file. Etiuda then trusts that key only: a team file signed with any other key is not used, including one handed over to a new lead. A value in any other form is ignored.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Etiuda trusts the lead of the team the desk joined.

If both this setting and "Set the team folder" are configured and either value is not valid, Etiuda uses neither.</string>
      <string id="DeskNoUpdateCheck">Turn off the check for a new version of Etiuda</string>
      <string id="DeskNoUpdateCheck_Explain">This policy setting stops Etiuda from checking for a new version.

If you enable this policy setting, Etiuda makes no request for its version note and shows no offer of a new version. Use this where new versions reach the computers by your own distribution.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Etiuda checks about once an hour and, when a newer version exists, offers it in the header's menu and in Settings.</string>
      <string id="StudioNoUpdateCheck">Turn off the check for a new version of Etiuda Studio</string>
      <string id="StudioNoUpdateCheck_Explain">This policy setting stops Etiuda Studio from checking for a new version.

If you enable this policy setting, Etiuda Studio makes no request for its version note and shows no offer of a new version. Use this where new versions reach the computers by your own distribution.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Etiuda Studio checks about once an hour and, when a newer version exists, offers it on the Overview, in the status bar and in About.</string>
      <string id="AiProvider">Set the AI service</string>
      <string id="AiProvider_Explain">This policy setting specifies the AI service Etiuda Studio may use to draft cards and bring in old replies, and Etiuda uses where "Use the organisation's AI model for the desk's search and suggestions" is enabled. Studio sends text to it only when the lead starts such a job and confirms what will be sent.

If you enable this policy setting, choose the service, or enter its name: openai, anthropic, google, azure or compatible. It stands over the service chosen in Studio's Settings, which then cannot be changed there. Any other value is ignored.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the service is chosen in Studio's Settings, and with none chosen Studio sends nothing to any AI service.</string>
      <string id="AiProvider_openai">OpenAI (openai)</string>
      <string id="AiProvider_anthropic">Anthropic (anthropic)</string>
      <string id="AiProvider_google">Google Gemini (google)</string>
      <string id="AiProvider_azure">Azure OpenAI (azure)</string>
      <string id="AiProvider_compatible">Another OpenAI-compatible service (compatible)</string>
      <string id="AiEndpoint">Set the AI service's address</string>
      <string id="AiEndpoint_Explain">This policy setting specifies the address to which Etiuda Studio, and Etiuda where "Use the organisation's AI model for the desk's search and suggestions" is enabled, send their requests to the AI service, such as your organisation's own gateway.

If you enable this policy setting, enter a full https address, such as https://ai.example.com/v1/, with no user name, query or fragment. It stands over the address entered in Studio's Settings, and Studio sends to no other. A value in any other form is ignored.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the address entered in Studio's Settings is used, or, where none is entered, the published address of OpenAI, Anthropic or Google. Azure OpenAI and other compatible services need an address.</string>
      <string id="AiModel">Set the AI model</string>
      <string id="AiModel_Explain">This policy setting specifies the model Etiuda Studio, and Etiuda where "Use the organisation's AI model for the desk's search and suggestions" is enabled, ask the AI service to use.

If you enable this policy setting, enter the model's name exactly as the service lists it. It stands over the model named in Studio's Settings.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the model is named in Studio's Settings. With no model named, Studio sends nothing.</string>
      <string id="AiKey">Set the AI service's key</string>
      <string id="AiKey_Explain">This policy setting specifies the key Etiuda Studio, and Etiuda where "Use the organisation's AI model for the desk's search and suggestions" is enabled, present to the AI service.

If you enable this policy setting, enter the key. It stands over the key kept in Studio's Settings. Both apps send this key only to the address set by "Set the AI service's address", or, where that is not set, to the published address of the service, and never to an address entered on the computer.

Warning: a key set by machine policy is stored in the registry, where every user of this computer can read it. Prefer a gateway address that needs no key, or a key that is limited to this use and can be withdrawn on its own.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the key is entered in Studio's Settings and kept sealed for that user's account.</string>
      <string id="DeskOrganisationModel">Use the organisation's AI model for the desk's search and suggestions</string>
      <string id="DeskOrganisationModel_Explain">This policy setting makes Etiuda rank its search and its intent suggestions with your organisation's AI model, in place of the model built into Etiuda.

If you enable this policy setting, Etiuda uses the service, address, model and key set by the four AI service policy settings in this template. The search text and the copied message the suggestions are made from are sent to that address, and a mark in Etiuda's header shows this on every screen. The choice cannot be changed in Etiuda's Settings. The person's own switches, "Suggest intents" and "Search by meaning", still turn ranking by meaning off, whichever model it is. When the organisation's model does not answer, the built-in model ranks meanwhile, sending nothing.

If you disable this policy setting, Etiuda uses the built-in model only, which works on this computer alone and sends nothing from it, and the choice cannot be changed in its Settings.

If you do not configure this policy setting, the model is chosen in Etiuda's Settings. The built-in model, the default, works on this computer alone and sends nothing from it.</string>
      <string id="Managed">Manage the accounts on this computer for the organisation</string>
      <string id="Managed_Explain">This policy setting marks this computer as managed by your organisation, which then decides who signs in to Etiuda and Etiuda Studio here, and with which account.

If you enable this policy setting, both programs show nothing to buy and no trial; offer no other account and no way to sign out, and keep the account that signed in, unless "Treat this computer as shared" is enabled; and hide everything that only the licence's owner may do. Personal accounts are not offered unless "Allow personal accounts" is enabled. Account, in each program, says that the organisation manages it. Everything else in both programs works as on any computer.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, both programs show their account settings as on any computer.</string>
      <string id="SharedComputer">Treat this computer as shared</string>
      <string id="SharedComputer_Explain">This policy setting lets more than one person use Etiuda and Etiuda Studio on this computer, one after another.

If you enable this policy setting on a computer where "Manage the accounts on this computer for the organisation" is enabled, signing out and signing in with another account are offered again, still within "Set the sign-in provider" and "Set the organisation's sign-in tenant".

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, a managed computer keeps the account that signed in on it.</string>
      <string id="AllowPersonalAccounts">Allow personal accounts</string>
      <string id="AllowPersonalAccounts_Explain">This policy setting decides whether a personal Microsoft account, or a Google account outside a Google Workspace domain, may sign in to Etiuda and Etiuda Studio on this computer.

If you enable this policy setting, personal accounts may sign in.

If you disable this policy setting, only work and school accounts may sign in: Microsoft's sign-in is asked for organisations' accounts alone, and a Google account must belong to a Google Workspace domain.

If you do not configure this policy setting, personal accounts may sign in, except where "Manage the accounts on this computer for the organisation" is enabled.</string>
      <string id="SigninProvider">Set the sign-in provider</string>
      <string id="SigninProvider_Explain">This policy setting limits sign-in to Etiuda and Etiuda Studio on this computer to one provider.

If you enable this policy setting, choose Microsoft or Google, or enter microsoft or google; only that provider is offered. Any other value offers no sign-in at all.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, both Microsoft and Google are offered.</string>
      <string id="SigninProvider_microsoft">Microsoft (microsoft)</string>
      <string id="SigninProvider_google">Google (google)</string>
      <string id="SigninTenant">Set the organisation's sign-in tenant</string>
      <string id="SigninTenant_Explain">This policy setting limits sign-in to Etiuda and Etiuda Studio on this computer to the accounts of one organisation.

If you enable this policy setting, enter your Microsoft Entra tenant ID, such as 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000, or your Google Workspace domain, such as example.com. Microsoft's sign-in then takes place at that tenant and Google's asks for that domain, and an account from anywhere else is refused even where the provider lets it sign in. A tenant ID allows Microsoft alone, and a domain Google alone. A value in any other form, or one that disagrees with "Set the sign-in provider", offers no sign-in at all.

For Microsoft, enter the tenant ID, never a domain: a domain such as contoso.com or contoso.onmicrosoft.com is read as a Google Workspace domain, so no Microsoft account can sign in.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the accounts of any organisation may sign in.</string>
      <string id="SupportContact">Set whom to ask for access</string>
      <string id="SupportContact_Explain">This policy setting names whom a person should ask when the organisation has not given their account access to Etiuda.

If you enable this policy setting, enter up to 200 characters, such as a service desk's name and telephone number. Etiuda and Etiuda Studio show it as written, after "To ask for access:", in place of the line that names the organisation's IT department, and never open it as a link.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, that line names the organisation's IT department.</string>
      <string id="NonPersistent">Keep each desk on a non-persistent desktop</string>
      <string id="NonPersistent_Explain">This policy setting tells Etiuda that this computer is a pooled or non-persistent desktop, such as a contact centre's virtual desktop, where a person may sign in on a different host each day.

Etiuda keeps a desk's identity in the person's profile, in %APPDATA%\etiuda, under keys Windows protects for that person. Where the profile keeps that folder and the person's Windows data protection keys, with an FSLogix Profile Container or a roaming profile, the desk is the same desk on every host and this setting changes nothing.

If you enable this policy setting, a desk whose own key cannot be opened on this profile is kept and said, not replaced: Etiuda says what happened and whom to ask, everything on the desk works as before, and no new desk is made unless "Let a non-persistent desktop make a new desk" is enabled. Each sign-in also says that the desk is pooled, so a person's pooled desks hold one place among their three computers, the newest taking it over, and their ordinary computers keep theirs.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, a desk whose key cannot be opened makes a new desk, as on any computer.</string>
      <string id="NonPersistentNewDesk">Let a non-persistent desktop make a new desk</string>
      <string id="NonPersistentNewDesk_Explain">This policy setting applies only with "Keep each desk on a non-persistent desktop".

If you enable this policy setting, a desk whose own key cannot be opened on this profile makes a new desk, as on any computer, and its team may need to let it in again. Its sign-ins still say that it is pooled, so it holds one place among the person's three computers.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, such a desk is kept and said, and makes no new desk.</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="TeamFolder">
        <textBox refId="TeamFolderBox">
          <label>Full path:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="LeadKey">
        <textBox refId="LeadKeyBox">
          <label>Public key (64 lowercase hexadecimal characters):</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="AiProvider">
        <dropdownList refId="AiProviderList" noSort="true">Service:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="AiEndpoint">
        <textBox refId="AiEndpointBox">
          <label>Address (https):</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="AiModel">
        <textBox refId="AiModelBox">
          <label>Model name:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="AiKey">
        <textBox refId="AiKeyBox">
          <label>Key:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="SigninProvider">
        <dropdownList refId="SigninProviderList" noSort="true">Provider:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="SigninTenant">
        <textBox refId="SigninTenantBox">
          <label>Tenant ID or Google Workspace domain:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="SupportContact">
        <textBox refId="SupportContactBox">
          <label>Whom to ask:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
